I concur... from trap.c:

void
drain_en(n)
register int n;
{
        if (!u.uenmax) return;
        You_feel("your magical energy drain away!");
        u.uen -= n;
        if(u.uen < 0)  {
                u.uenmax += u.uen;
                if(u.uenmax < 0) u.uenmax = 0;
                u.uen = 0;
        }
        flags.botl = 1;
}

When you are at Pw:0(0), u.uenmax == 0, thus if (!u.uenmax) is true
and the function returns without doing anything further.  XL1 Arcs
start with at least 2 Pw, more with higher INT...

